  "description": "The Rush was built for riders who want a real track-inspired frame that still makes sense in the street. Fast, responsive, and unmistakably lively, it feels just as at home carving through city traffic and rough pavement as it does rolling laps at the velodrome.\n\nThis latest version opens up tire clearance for modern fixed riding and light tracklocross duty, while preserving the sharp geometry and direct handling that made the Rush a cult favorite. Riders consistently describe it as stiff when you put power down, yet smoother and more composed than most aluminum or cheaper steel frames.\n\nAn expertly butted chromoly tubeset with side-tacked seatstays and S-bend chainstays offer a smooth stylish ride. To cap off its Keirin-inspired look, we continue to match the Rush with a threaded fork for clean, classic look and more bar height adjustment.\n\nRevised geometry. We have one fewer size this time. And the size 48cm is more like a 51/53cm for someone with shorter legs than a true 48cm.\n\nNote: If you are running brakes, you will need 57mm reach (mid-reach) not 49mm reach calipers. That's just a needed change to allow bigger tires.\n\nInvestment cast Tange horizontal track fork ends\n\nDrilled for caliper brakes\n\n48, 53, 55, 57, 60cm (Center to top of seat collar)\n\n*Decals sit under the clearcoat this time",
